/-!
# Two movers, frozen readings [1, 2, 5, 6]: the landing for ALL movers beyond the least frozen reading, in whichever lonely piece holds it (GENERATED by `s2later_gen_v1.py`)

Written 2026-10-23.  New file.  Lonely pieces of the frozen set from `1/(8·1)` (exact), indexed from 0: [1/8, 7/48], [9/40, 5/16].
* `landL1256_<j>`: for ANY `d1, d2 > 0`, IF no piece `i < j` holds a common clear instant of the two movers and piece `j` does, THEN the first lonely
  instant `T` of the frozen set with both movers exists, lies in piece `j`, and is the first common clear instant at or after its left end (the movers-only
  cascade fixed point from the left end of piece `j`).  Earlier pieces are excluded by the hypothesis, the gaps by `fnot`, later pieces by order.
* `exists_union_1256`: for ALL real `d1, d2 > 1` some piece `j ≤ 1` holds a common clear instant (finite box cover of `{d1 ≤ d2}`: `13` columns in `d1`, `36` boxes;
  box kinds (kind, piece): {"('P', 0)": 9, "('P', 1)": 13, "('R1a', 0)": 3, "('R1a', 1)": 10, "('R1b', 1)": 1}; `d1 > 12` by `big_both` in piece 1 [PROVISIONAL: counting tool]).
* `land2_later_1256`: the assembled statement, no grid, no upper threshold.  No nonexistence of a common clear instant is proved for any box: the case split is on the
  statement itself (`by_cases` on each piece in turn).
Grades: [L]; the existence statement is discharged by a finite box cover [PROVISIONAL: covering]; `r1_rect`/`big_both` are [PROVISIONAL: counting tool].
Not proved here: the cascade's path inside the piece; movers at or below `1`.
-/

